    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, exposed as a read-only field on the owner response.\n\nThe logic is split by responsibility rather than concentrated in one place:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-purpose utility holding the standard Luhn algorithm (`Luhn.checkDigit(String)`), ignoring non-digit characters. This mirrors the existing `MembershipLevels` / `Postcodes` utility pattern and keeps the algorithm reusable and independently testable.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit(Owner)` derivation method (returning `null` before a customer code is assigned) and a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)`, alongside the other derived fields like `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`. The mapper delegates to `Luhn` rather than embedding the arithmetic.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
